eeu 1.0.1 (2026-11-19)
- fix line-buffer resizing when splitting long lines
- reject overflowing or undersized line-buffer capacity calculations
- safely parse .init.ee lines, including missing final newline and overlong lines
- replace fixed-size path expansion buffers with dynamically sized storage
- reject final-component symlinks and non-regular files when saving
- check write, flush, sync, and close errors before reporting a successful save
- enforce restricted mode in finish() and write_file()
- close file descriptors after reading and retry interrupted reads
- dynamically allocate print command buffers
- safely back up and open the editor configuration file
- add core regression tests for resizing, config parsing, and path expansion

eeu 1.0.0 (2026-11-17)
- first independently versioned eeu release based on FreeBSD 15.1 ee sources
- UTF-8 input, display, cursor movement, deletion, prompts, and search
- terminal-cell width handling for Unicode code points
- Russian menus, help, prompts, status text, and diagnostics via catgets
- editor commands and configuration keywords remain English
- message catalog basename is eeu (share/nls/<locale>/eeu)
- retain the original ee and ree programs and their configuration names
- improve allocation failure handling in line resizing and catalog strings
- default build/test locale follows NLS_LOCALE for FreeBSD systems configured for Russian

version 1.5.0 (2/16/2009)
- added display of line number, column, and lines from top to separator line
  for info window
- minor changes to reduce number of warnings when using -pedantic option

version 1.4.7 (2/10/2009)
- changed how strings are terminated from the old usage of NULL to the current
  use of character zero, '\0'
- changed the licensing since the Artistic License is now considered
  restrictive

version 1.4.6
- modified new_curse.c to handle different subdirectory naming in terminfo
  directory; first noted on Mac OS 10.2

version 1.4.5a (12/23/2001)
- modified get_options to be cleaner for arg handling

version 1.4.5 (12/15/2001)
- made changes to check usage of arguments provided so that if a file is
  specified options are no longer accepted (that is, they are treated as file
  names)
- changed to use ee_version.h to allow changing version number without need
  to change ee.c directly

version 1.4.4 (8/17/2001)
- added code to check if the parent process has died, and if so to exit
  gracefully

version 1.4.3 (6/25/2001)
- modified create.make and new_curse.c to allow defining TERMCAP file
  location (since some distributions move the termcap file)
- source directory now has version number attached to directory name

version 1.4.2 (1/19/2001)
- change to create.make script to add unistd.h to files to search for
  select() declaration
- change to new_curse.c for proper raw mode operation
